Mouse Bindings
	Mouse bindings in Edit mode :
	
	Left button : 
			When pressed in a primitive widget,
			selects this widget and unselects all
			previously selected widgets. The
			selected widget becomes the "current"
			widget.
	
			When pressed in a top-level composite
			widget, unselects all widgets.
	
			The selection can be moved by keeping
			the left button pressed and moving the
			mouse.
	
	Middle button :
			Pop the Resources box.
	
	Control-middle button :
			Pop the Edit Resource Box.
	
	Control-left button :
			When pressed in a primitive widget,
			adds this widget to the selection.
			The selected widget becomes the "current"
			widget.
	
	Right button :
			Selects the parent of the current widget.
			This is used to select composite widgets
			that cannot be selected directly using
			the left button.
	
		
Keyboard Bindings
	Default keyboard bindings in Edit mode :
	
	^X :	Cut the selection into the cut-buffer.If there is
		no selection, cut the object which is located
		under the cursor.
	
	^C :	Copy the selection into the cut-buffer. If there is
		no selection, copy the object which is located
		under the cursor.
	
	^P :	Paste the contents of the cut-buffer. The contents
		must be dragged to the desired location.
	
	^K :	Delete the selection. If there is no selection,
		delete the object which is located under the cursor.
	
	^U :	Undo the last "undoable" command.
	
	^D :	Duplicate the selection. If there is no selection,
		duplicate the object which is located under the cursor.
	
	^T :	Switch to Try mode.
	
	The default keyboard bindings can be overriden
	on the xfm command line. For details enter xfm -help.
